# Local run state written while the app is running. Tailwind v4 scans every
# non-ignored file, so a run written here full-reloads every open Workbench tab and
# throws away whatever conversation or unsaved edit was on screen.
.agent-runs/
.frontend-verify/

# Same reason, plus a second one: a headless run started from the Workbench touches
# files in here while it works, and every touch reloads the page the run was started
# from. A worktree is also a second copy of the whole app, so Tailwind scans it and
# Biome lints it, and every finding duplicates a file nobody is editing.
.claude/*
!.claude/launch.json
!.claude/skills/

# Appended by the session hooks on every run start/end, which reloads open tabs
# through the same Tailwind scan (and keeps git status permanently dirty).
# Untracked like CODEBASE.md; the hooks keep writing it on disk regardless.
SESSION-JOURNAL.md
